{"summary": "I finished `transpose(text)` in `transpose.py`, and it gives the right output for the examples I tried.

It goes through the lines from the bottom up and pads each line with spaces on the right, only up to the length of the longest line below it. Then it builds each output row from one column. Because of this, shorter rows get spaces on the left, nothing gets spaces added on the right, and spaces that were in the input stay where they were.

I ran a short `python -c` check. `ABC\nDE` gave `AD\nBE\nC`, `AB\nDEF` gave `AD\nBE\n F`, empty input gave an empty string, and the triangle example gave the expected staircase of `TEASER` lines. The project has no test files, so the hidden tests haven't been run here.", "outputs": ["transpose.py"]}
